# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# `biome.json` sets `lineEnding: "lf"`, so a CRLF working tree fails `pnpm lint` on every file at
# once. Windows checkouts default to `core.autocrlf=true`, which produces exactly that: the format
# check reports the entire tree as misformatted, for a reason no diff will show and that reproduces
# on no other platform.
#
# Declared here rather than left to each contributor's git config, because the requirement belongs
# to the repository. `.editorconfig` states the same rule for editors, so a file is authored with
# LF and checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never inspected or rewritten as text.
*.png binary
